Read `postech-ai-helper/ai/agent-bootstrap.md` (resolve relative to the workspace root `$(HOME)/git/fiap/postech-sw-architecture/`) and follow it. This repo and `postech-ai-helper` are sibling repos under that workspace root -- do **not** resolve the path relative to this file's directory or this repo's root.

That bootstrap file is the single source of truth for what every AI agent must do in this workspace -- session start, task end, commit workflow, memory protocol.

Project-specific accumulated learnings (decisions, conventions, gotchas, tech debt) live in `MEMORY.md` at this repo's root. Read it after the bootstrap.

If `postech-ai-helper/` is not present as a sibling under the workspace root, **stop and ask the user to clone it** (`gh repo clone fiap-postech-sw-architecture/postech-ai-helper` from the workspace root) before doing any work. The canonical rules are required.
